1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,458
Without Einstein,

2
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:03,440
the colour gold would be silver.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,190
Almost every metal is silvery grey.

4
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:10,060
Gold is one of the very few that isn't.

5
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,596
Gold's nucleus has 79 protons.

6
00:00:13,596 --> 00:00:20,020
They whip its innermost electrons around at about 58% of the speed of light.

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,319
At that speed, relativity kicks in.

8
00:00:23,319 --> 00:00:25,134
The electrons act heavier,

9
00:00:25,134 --> 00:00:26,820
and their orbits shrink.

10
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:30,633
That shift lets gold absorb blue light.

11
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:33,048
Silver only absorbs ultraviolet,

12
00:00:33,048 --> 00:00:34,540
which we can't see.

13
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:37,345
Take blue out of white light,

14
00:00:37,345 --> 00:00:40,050
and what's left looks yellow. That's gold.

15
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:42,272
Without relativity,

16
00:00:42,272 --> 00:00:44,414
gold would reflect every colour,

17
00:00:44,414 --> 00:00:45,610
just like silver.

18
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:51,450
So every gold ring you've ever seen is a little piece of relativity.
